---
import { DOCS, PRICING, REPO_URL, SHIPPED, TRIAL } from "../config";
import SectionHeader from "./SectionHeader.astro";

/**
 * The price, and the two things that make it defensible rather than awkward:
 * the ladder is published in advance, and there are two separate ways to find
 * out whether this is for you before you commit.
 *
 * Those two are not interchangeable and the copy must not blur them. The trial
 * answers "does this work against MY mail" — technical, asked first, and the
 * only honest answer to it is running the thing. The refund answers "was it
 * worth the money" — commercial, asked afterwards. EULA §3 opens on exactly
 * this distinction and this section mirrors it.
 *
 * This page used to claim that compiling the source needed no licence key. It
 * is not true: the gate in `ServerHost.swift` runs on `Entitlement.current`,
 * which knows licensed / trial / refused and nothing whatever about how the
 * binary was produced. A reader who acted on it would have spent an evening
 * reaching the same refusal. Do not reintroduce it in any form — the fee was
 * never the point, the key is.
 *
 * Nothing here renders a buy button until SHIPPED.
 */
const included = [
  `A ${TRIAL.minutes}-minute trial, every surface at full function. Press the button; nothing arms itself.`,
  "Every 1.x release, free. 2.0 is a new purchase; nothing lapses in between.",
  "Every Mac you own or control. No activation limit and nothing counts your installs.",
  `${PRICING.refundDays} days to change your mind, for any reason or none.`,
  "No account, no login, no phone-home. The key verifies on your Mac and nowhere else.",
];
---

<section id="pricing" class="wrap scroll-mt-20 py-[96px]">
  <SectionHeader
    eyebrow="Price"
    heading="Pay once.<br />Then it is yours."
  >
    One Full Disk Access grant, held by a notarized binary from an identifiable developer, instead of
    four grants handed out to whichever editors happened to spawn a server. The servers themselves
    stay MIT and free forever.
  </SectionHeader>

  <div class="reveal rounded-[16px] border border-rule bg-bg-2 p-6 sm:p-9">
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-8 lg:flex-row lg:items-start lg:gap-12">
      <div class="flex flex-none flex-col gap-3 lg:w-[240px]">
        <div class="font-display text-[44px] leading-none font-semibold tracking-[-0.04em]">
          {PRICING.price}
        </div>
        <div class="text-[14px] leading-[1.6] text-fg-dim">
          One time, for all of 1.x. Not a subscription.
        </div>
        {/* Both figures, because they are not a conversion of each other: the
            dollar price is quoted tax-exclusive and the euro one VAT-inclusive,
            as each side is normally quoted. Showing only the first would leave
            an EU buyer without the total they are actually charged. */}
        <div class="text-[13.5px] leading-[1.6] text-fg-dim">
          {PRICING.eur.price} in the EU, VAT included.
        </div>

        {
          SHIPPED ? (
            <a
              href={PRICING.buy}
              class="mt-1 rounded-[10px] bg-accent px-[22px] py-3 text-center text-[14.5px] font-medium text-accent-ink transition-colors hover:bg-accent-hi"
            >
              Buy a licence
            </a>
          ) : (
            <div class="mono mt-1 !text-fg-dim">Not on sale yet</div>
          )
        }
      </div>

      <ul class="m-0 flex list-none flex-col gap-3 p-0">
        {
          included.map((line) => (
            <li class="flex gap-3 text-[14.5px] leading-[1.6] text-pretty text-fg-dim">
              <span class="flex-none text-accent" aria-hidden="true">
                ·
              </span>
              {line}
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="mono mt-12 mb-6">The ladder, published in advance</div>
  <dl class="m-0 grid grid-cols-1 gap-0">
    {
      PRICING.ladder.map((rung) => (
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-1.5 border-t border-rule py-5 last:border-b sm:grid-cols-[120px_180px_1fr] sm:gap-8">
          <dt class="text-[14px] font-medium text-fg">{rung.price}</dt>
          <dd class="m-0 text-[14px] leading-[1.6] text-fg-dim">{rung.when}</dd>
          <dd class="m-0 text-[14px] leading-[1.6] text-pretty text-fg-muted">{rung.covers}</dd>
        </div>
      ))
    }
  </dl>
  <p class="mt-6 mb-0 max-w-[62ch] text-[14px] leading-[1.65] text-pretty text-fg-muted">
    The price rises when a surface lands, never because time passed — and once risen it does not come
    back down. Buying early is the whole of the discount.
  </p>

  <p class="mt-10 mb-0 max-w-[62ch] text-[14px] leading-[1.65] text-pretty text-fg-dim">
    <strong class="font-medium text-fg">Run the servers on their own and pay nothing.</strong>{" "}
    The
    <a
      href={REPO_URL}
      target="_blank"
      rel="noopener"
      class="text-accent transition-colors hover:text-accent-hi">servers</a
    > are MIT and always were — they need no key, and they do the work. What a licence buys is the app:
    the signed and notarized binary that holds one Full Disk Access grant on their behalf, and the work
    of keeping it working. Its source is public for a reason that has nothing to do with price: nobody
    should grant Full Disk Access to software they cannot read. Read it, build it, run your own — the
    <a
      href={DOCS.appLicense}
      target="_blank"
      rel="noopener"
      class="text-accent transition-colors hover:text-accent-hi">licence</a
    > is explicit that any build asks for a key, rather than leaving you to find out at the first run.
  </p>

  <p class="mt-6 mb-0 max-w-[62ch] text-[14px] leading-[1.65] text-pretty text-fg-muted">
    The trial is held in memory and never written to disk, so quitting Cupertino and opening it again
    starts another one. Nothing stops you and nothing pretends to. When the window closes it closes
    properly: the servers it started are stopped, and your assistant reports a dropped connection.
    A deadline named on the button that started it is not a window if it cannot shut.
  </p>
</section>
